Iskra's change to the vendored photocraft-paint, applied by scripts/vendor.sh after each copy.

StrokeRenderer::coverage_in read every pixel through coverage_at: three hash-map lookups
(coverage, depth, Dual Brush) per pixel. Iskra's LiveStroke calls it over every redone tile
on every frame, and with a large scattered brush that was 60 % of a frame. It now looks each
coverage tile up once and reads its pixels in place, giving the same values (6x faster for
a 404 px brush, measured with crates/drawing/examples/stroke_lag.rs).

Worth offering upstream; drop this file once PhotoCraft has an equivalent.

diff --git a/crates/third_party/photocraft/paint/src/render.rs b/crates/third_party/photocraft/paint/src/render.rs
